 !!! Note
     The minimum last stake amount can be configured using `last_stake_amount_min_ratio` - which defaults to 0.5 (50%). This means that the minimum stake amount that's ever used is `stake_amount * 0.5`. This avoids very low stake amounts, that are close to the minimum tradable amount for the pair and can be refused by the exchange.
 
+#### Currency exposure limit
+
+If several of your pairs settle in the same currency (for example, several USDT-margined futures, or several coins quoted in the same stablecoin), a large move in that currency can hit several open trades at once, even though each individual trade looked fine in isolation.
+
+`max_currency_exposure` limits the combined stake committed to all simultaneously open trades that settle in the same currency to a configurable share of the total tradable capital, regardless of how many individual trades that's spread across.
+
+Assuming a tradable balance of 1000 USDT and `max_currency_exposure=0.5`, the bot will never let the combined stake of open trades settling in USDT exceed 500 USDT, even if `max_open_trades` and the available balance would otherwise allow more. When opening (or increasing) a trade would push the combined exposure over this limit, the trade is skipped, or sized down to fit under the limit - the same way the bot already handles other stake-sizing limits, and identically whether running live/dry-run or backtesting.
+
+*Defaults to `1.0` (100%), which disables this additional check.*
+
 #### Static stake amount
 
 The `stake_amount` configuration statically configures the amount of stake-currency your bot will use for each trade.
